.Dd August 31, 2026
.Dt TDX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tdx
.Nd Turbo Debugger X — native Linux debugger for DOS EXE/COM
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op options
.Op Ar file.exe|file.com
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads a DOS MZ EXE or .COM into an 8086 real-mode machine (Unicorn),
shows a Turbo Debugger–like CPU window (SDL2) and an optional CGA user
screen, and listens on a UNIX socket for agent commands.
.Pp
Options and the input path may appear in any order.
With no arguments,
.Nm
prints this usage text.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--symbols PATH"
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Show version and exit.
.It Fl -no-ui
Headless (no SDL windows).
.It Fl -no-game
Do not open the CGA window.
.It Fl -no-sock
Do not listen on the agent socket.
.It Fl -sock Ar PATH
Agent socket (default
.Pa /tmp/tdx.sock ).
.It Fl -run
Run until break or halt after load.
.El
.Sh KEYS
F7 trace, F8 step over, F9 run/pause, F2 breakpoint, Alt-X quit.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Nm tdxctl
.Sh AUTHORS
TDX / librex
